From: PupJune2 <PupJune2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: CromIKO for Windows: CromIKO DNS
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The CromIKO DNS screen of the Android app (CromIKO-DNS-Screen.patch and
CromIKO-DNS-Shortcut.patch) in the settings of the desktop version
(Settings > Privacy and security > Security), instead of the switch and
the drop-down of secure DNS:

- An animated orbit (cromiko_dns_orbit.ts, drawn like the Android one):
  the DNS icon glows in the middle of orbits like the ring of the mascot,
  queries go round them and stars of the logo twinkle. Off, it is gray and
  still; with "reduce motion" it stands still.
- A big status: "Protected" with the provider, "Protected when possible"
  (automatic) or "CromIKO DNS is off", with the notices of managed
  browsers and parental controls.
- "Test connection" checks that the provider answers, with waves from the
  middle of the orbit, and shows how fast ("Connected • 42 ms") or that it
  can't be reached.
- The providers as cards with a letter in a CromIKO color, what they
  filter as a colored tag (blocks ads and trackers, family filter, blocks
  malware, no filtering) and "Recommended" on Quad9, the default. They are
  in the order of the Android screen instead of a random one: Quad9, then
  the ones that block ads, the family filters, the ones that block malware
  and the unfiltered ones, with "Automatic" and "Custom" (and its address
  field). Only the chosen card shows until "Choose another provider".
- Everything takes the colors of the theme, so it follows the accent
  color, in light and dark.
- "CromIKO DNS" in the app menu, under the Fire button, with the CromIKO
  DNS icon (drawn from the logo by tools/cromiko/gen_feature_icons.py),
  opens the security settings at CromIKO DNS.

It stores the same settings as before and keeps the checks of a custom
address.

